<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Doc 1: (Title: List of Starship launches - Wikipedia) … mission slated for launch to the moon in 2027 as part of SpaceX’s first Starship HLS mission for the Artemis program. An unknown number of refueling …</span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Doc 2: (Title: SpaceX Starship - Wikipedia) The first launch of a full Starship vehicle occurred on April 20, 2023, and ended with the explosion of the rocket four minutes after liftoff. The program has …</span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Doc 3: (Title: Artemis I - NASA) Launch date: Nov. 16, 2022 ; Mission duration: 25 days, 10 hours, 53 minutes ; Total distance traveled: 1.4 million miles ; Re-entry speed: 24,581 mph (Mach 32).</span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Doc 4: (Title: Starship overview - SpaceX) Starship is the world’s most powerful launch vehicle ever developed, capable of carrying up to 150 metric tonnes fully reusable and 250 metric tonnes expendable …</span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Doc 5: (Title: NASA’s Artemis Moon Missions: all you need to know) Artemis 1: After being delayed four times, Artemis 1 successfully launched on Wednesday 16 November 2022 at 1:47am EST (6:47am GMT); Artemis 2: No earlier than …</span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/response&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;think&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">Starship’s first launch was on 2023-04-20, and Artemis I launched on 2022-11-16. I’ll calculate the difference using Python datetime.</span>&lt;/think&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.10.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;code&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> 
<br class="ltx_break"></span>import datetime 
<br class="ltx_break">first_launch = datetime.datetime(2023, 4, 20) 
<br class="ltx_break">artemis_i = datetime.datetime(2022, 11, 16) 
<br class="ltx_break">days = (artemis_i - first_launch).days 
<br class="ltx_break">print(days) 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.11.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span>&lt;/code&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.11.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;response&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">-155 
<br class="ltx_break"></span>&lt;/response&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.12.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;answer&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">155</span>&lt;/answer&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.13.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> 
