<section id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Case 2.2</h4>

<div id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Question: Compute the GDP growth rate of India from the fiscal year 2021 to 2024. (Unit: percentage, round to one decimal place)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="674.06" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-337.03px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 700 674.06" width="700"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,674.06) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FF6666;" fill="#FF6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 674.06 L 700 674.06 L 700 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFE6E6;" fill="#FFE6E6" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 1.97 L 1.97 648.41 L 698.03 648.41 L 698.03 1.97 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFCCCC;" fill="#FFCCCC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 650.38 L 1.97 672.09 L 698.03 672.09 L 698.03 650.38 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 657.77)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:41.27em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="571.06"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:41.27em;">
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Qwen2.5-Instruct-7B + SE/CI</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:47.46em;--ltx-fo-height:45.01em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="622.83" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 622.83)" width="656.71"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:47.46em;">
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;think&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
To compute the GDP growth rate from fiscal year 2021 to 2024 for India, I need to gather the GDP values for these years. Then, I can use the formula for calculating the growth rate:
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Growth Rate}=\left(\frac{\text{GDP}_{\text{Year 2}}-\text{GDP}_{\text{Year 1}}}{\text{GDP}_{\text{Year 1}}}\right)\times 100" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Growth Rate</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msub><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">GDP</mtext><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Year 2</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">GDP</mtext><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Year 1</mtext></msub></mrow><msub><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">GDP</mtext><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Year 1</mtext></msub></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Growth Rate}=\left(\frac{\text{GDP}_{\text{Year 2}}-\text{GDP}_{\text{Year 1}}}{\text{GDP}_{\text{Year 1}}}\right)\times 100</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">I will assume that the GDP figures are in constant prices and in billions of local currency units for simplicity, as the exact currency is not specified.
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/think&gt;</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;search&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">GDP of India 2021-2024</span>&lt;/search&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;response&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Doc 1: (Title: Economy of India - Wikipedia) Economy of India ; –6.4% of GDP (2022–23) · 34.96 trillion (US$410 billion); (2025–26) · 50.65 trillion (US$600 billion); (2025–26) · Donor: Increase $4.234 …</span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Doc 2: (Title: GDP (current US$) - India - World Bank Data) GDP (current US$) - India. Country official statistics, National Statistical Organizations and/or Central Banks; National Accounts data files, Organisation …</span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Doc 3: (Title: India GDP — Historical Chart &amp; Data - Macrotrends) India GDP for 2022 was 3.353 trillion US dollars, a 5.88% increase from 2021. · India GDP for 2021 was 3.167 trillion US dollars, a 18.41% increase from 2020.</span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Doc 4: (Title: India Fiscal Year GDP Growth - Trading Economics) Full Year GDP Growth in India decreased to 6.50 percent in 2025 from 9.20 percent in 2024. Full Year GDP Growth in India averaged 6.42 percent from 2006 until …</span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Doc 5: (Title: India - IMF DataMapper) Real GDP growth. Annual percent change. 6.2 ; GDP, current prices. Billions of U.S. dollars. 4.19 ; GDP per capita, current prices. U.S. dollars per capita. 2.88.</span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/response&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;code&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> 
<br class="ltx_break"></span># Define the GDP values in trillions of Indian Rupees<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.11.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> 
<br class="ltx_break"></span>gdp_2021 = 31.67<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.11.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.11.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFF00;">gdp_2024 = 41.00</span> <span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.11.1.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B30000;">(Hallucination !)</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"># Calculate the growth rate<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> 
<br class="ltx_break"></span>growth_rate = ((gdp_2024 - gdp_2021) / gdp_2021) * 100<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.12.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> 
<br class="ltx_break"></span>print(f"growth_rate:.1f%")<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.12.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> 
<br class="ltx_break"></span>&lt;/code&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.12.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;response&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">29.5% 
<br class="ltx_break"></span>&lt;/response&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.13.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;answer&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">29.5</span>&lt;/answer&gt;<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.14.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> 
<span id="A3.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.pic1.2.14.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block fa fa-times" aria-hidden="true">
</span>
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
