<span id="A3.SSx3.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx3.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Doc 1: (Title: List of World Organization of the Scout Movement members) The World Organization of the Scout Movement is the largest international scout organization and was established in 1922. It has 176 members.</span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx3.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx3.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Doc 2: (Title: Scouting Countries) This is a complete list of the countries where Scouting exists. The asterisks mark countries that have third-party operating agreements with the US.</span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx3.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx3.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Doc 3: (Title: Scouts - World Scouting) There are currently more than 50 million Scouts, both young people and adults, across 216 countries and territories. Internationally recognised National Scout …</span></span>
<span id="A3.SSx3.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx3.SSSx1.p3.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Doc 4: (Title: Scouting in Other Countries 2025 - World Population Review) Just about every country in the world, with a few notable exceptions, has a scouting program. Although there are several scouting programs globally, only about …</span></span>
